The files are unmodified copies (equal to upstream after Git's line-ending normalisation; the
WebAssembly file is byte-identical); pinned commits and hashes are recorded in the PROVENANCE.md file
of each directory. "Derived from" these projects, not endorsed by their authors.

Not vendored

The Lean development (lean/) uses no Mathlib and has no Lean package dependencies; it needs only the
Lean 4 toolchain named in lean/lean-toolchain, which elan downloads.

The Python programs use packages installed by pip and not copied into this repository:
python-sat (PySAT 1.9.dev21, MIT licence), OR-Tools (Apache 2.0), NumPy and NetworkX (BSD 3-Clause).
python-sat bundles the two SAT solvers used by this project: Glucose 4.1 (MIT licence) and
CaDiCaL 1.9.5 (MIT licence). The exact versions used are in requirements.txt and
results/run_all.json. Each package and each bundled solver keeps its own licence.

The Eshkol compiler, Node.js and gcc are used as installed tools and are not part of this repository.
